t / C++ Game Systems\n\nCore\nWorkflows, Automation, Tooling\nAI\n\nMy point on AI: it should not be used as an artistic tool but as a multiplier for code...\n\n...\n\nMy point on AI: it should not be used as an artistic tool, and it should not replace the technical learning that turns someone into an artist. AI is cold. It is a machine without empathy, and that is how it should be considered.\n\nPointing it at psychology, love or art is a bad idea. Those things do not run on probabilities, so what comes back is usually poor, and the cost is real: the user's time, energy, compute, and a certain ethical awareness. Use it only on what matters.\n\nReading books and exercising critical thinking matter more and more in the age of AI. I am not saying that thinking is more important than AI. I am saying that AI is no reason to stop thinking, and that a model summarising a book is no reason to stop reading it. That would be a mistake.\n\nLearning a language is the clearest example. Speaking it in the street takes skill, memory and constant practice. So keep learning things without AI as a crutch, or the muscles of your brain waste away, and in the end you stop making choices at all: even artistic choices get worse when those muscles go unused. Keep your own way of thinking and your own way of reaching knowledge, through works and books rather than through a model. And works means many things: games, films, books, comics, a podcast on YouTube.\n\nThen use AI as a multiplier, for code and development, because it is excellent at that. Agentic tools like Cursor, Claude Code and ChatGPT are mature enough to build robust programs, and insisting on writing everything by hand would be a mistake. It does require knowing exactly what you are doing, and getting better at it.\n\nWhat matters most is to keep learning alongside AI rather than only with it: think outside the model first, then bring your own thesis to it.\n\nROLE\n\nWhat is my role: Tech Art is a multiplier a bridge for art and code...\n\n...\n\nWhat is my role: Tech Art is a multiplier, a bridge bridging art, especially in 3D, and computer systems automation.\n\nBuild accessible tools for artists, designers, and users.\nCreate reusable systems.\nBoost performance without compromising visuals.\nAvailable for Freelance, Houdini, UE5\nSee more\n\nWhether you're a AAA studio or an indie team, I solve pipeline challenges, build custom tools, and craft environments that tell stories. Every project is an opportunity to push the craft forward through design, tech art, and programming.\n\nI'm looking to collaborate with ambitious, optimistic teams on projects that make an impact.\n\nBreakdown - FLEUR DE LYS\nTrim Sheet Height - FLEUR DE LYS\nPetals Height - FLEUR DE LYS\nCeramic Tiles - Made with Houdini Copernicus and Unreal Lumen.\nBrowse more\n3D\nHOUDINI · UNREAL\nFleur de Lys: Procedural Lily, Houdini to Unreal\nHOUDINI · COPERNICUS\nCeramic Tiles - Made with Houdini Copernicus and Unreal Lumen\nHOUDINI · CHURCH\nHDA Stairs Component\nHOUDINI\nUV Texture Variation Offset\nMODELING LOUISIANA BAYOU\nLouisiana Bayou Church\nHOUDINI\nProcedural Shutters in Houdini\nHOUDINI · RIZOMUV · SUBSTANCE · UE5\nHero Asset Texturing Pipeline\nHOUDINI · UNREAL ENGINE 5\nAsset Scattering & Placement\nHOUDINI · SUBSTANCE · UE5\nProcedural Grass System\nUNREAL ENGINE 5\nMaterial Layer System\nUNREAL ENGINE 5\nLouisiana Bayou V1.5\nSUBSTANCE DESIGNER\nTexturing Cliff\nSUBSTANCE DESIGNER\nSubstance Ornate Fabric Introduction\nPROCEDURAL ENVIRONMENTS\nHoudini Game Environments\nPROCEDURAL MODELING\nWater Wheel\nVFX / GROOMING\nNiagara Vortex VFX\nHOUDINI POINT VOP\nProcedural Rock Gen\nHOUDINI HDA\nPampa Grass\nCode / Design\nUX / UI\nZenRayProgress Design Tour\nUNREAL ENGINE\nMetaHuman Markerless macOS Plugin\nMACOS APP\nZenRay Dictate App\nAPP\nZenRayProgress App\nPRESENTATION TOOL\nMagickSlides\nSUBSTANCE DESIGNER MCP\nSubstance Designer MCP Plugin\nPYTHON TOOL\nPushVault\nUNREAL ENGINE 5\nUE5 MCP Plugin\